# Clean system-integration test gate

Before every test involving Siri, Spotlight, App Intents, Shortcuts, signing, installation, or
another operating-system service:

1. Inventory running related processes, installed test bundles, bundle identifiers, versions, and
   launch paths.
2. Quit only the identified test processes and remove or isolate only validated duplicate test
   bundles. Never touch a user's normal production application.
3. Keep exactly one named test bundle per experiment and record its path, bundle identifier,
   version, signing state, and launch state.
4. Launch that bundle cleanly, confirm its runtime registration/index status, then run one
   documented test phrase or interaction.
5. Treat evidence from a mixed or stale environment as invalid. Do not request a user retest
   until this preflight is recorded.
